---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="How AI Runs Here turns hands-on Applied AI experiments into clear, evidence-aware field notes."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="about-hero__main">
        <p class="eyebrow">About this lab notebook</p>
        <h1 class="display" id="about-title">Learn by building. Explain by showing.</h1>
        <p class="about-hero__intro">
          I’m Li, a Technical Marketing Manager focused on Applied AI in OpenShift. This site turns that learning work
          into practical, evidence-aware field notes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="about-hero__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Editorial rule</p>
        <p>Say what was tested, name the environment, preserve the useful failure, and mark what still needs verification.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="section-block">
      <div class="method-grid">
        <section class="method-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
          <h2>Build before explaining</h2>
          <p>
            Each field note begins with a real question, a lab, or a troubleshooting session. The useful outcome is not
            only the final command—it is the reasoning, evidence, and recovery path that make the result repeatable.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="method-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Audience</p>
          <h2>Meet readers where they are</h2>
          <p>
            AI Runs Here is for developers, platform engineers, technical sellers, customers, and curious beginners
            learning how Applied AI fits into OpenShift. Concepts start in plain language and keep the technical detail
            needed to try them.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="method-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
          <h2>Accuracy is an ongoing practice</h2>
          <p>
            Product behavior and lab environments change. When a note needs correction, the goal is to update it
            clearly, retain relevant version context, and distinguish a confirmed result from an expectation or an
            experiment still in progress.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="method-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Independence</p>
          <h2>A personal learning publication</h2>
          <p>
            This site may discuss Red Hat products, including OpenShift, but it reflects a personal learning process. AI
            Runs Here is not an official Red Hat website, and product documentation remains the source of record.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
